    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d360">

                <pb facs="0438" n="334" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg334"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/4159: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Shanghai (Cunningham)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-15T11:00:00-05:00">February 15, 1932—11
                        a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>29. For the confidential information and guidance of the Minister and the Consul
                    General.</p>
                <p>Your 43, February 13, 1 p.m., in regard to aviation gasoline.</p>
                <p>Department approves your position in the matter.</p>
                <p>Department emphasizes again, however, the desirability of cooperating with your
                    British colleague in reference to all such matters and <pb facs="0439" n="335"
                        xml:id="pg335"/> endeavoring to work out with him, where practicable and
                    possible, a common course.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
